### Analysis: Detecting and Skipping Symlinks

- [x] Gather context - read `pipeline.ts` and related files
- [x] Analyze symlink detection approach
- [x] Provide recommendations

---

### Root Cause

`pipeline.ts` itself doesn't need changes — it just orchestrates phases. The actual bug lives in **`gitnexus/src/core/ingestion/filesystem-walker.ts`**, which is the only place that touches the filesystem.

**The problematic code (lines 20–24):**
```ts
const files = await glob('**/*', {
  cwd: repoPath,
  nodir: true,
  dot: false,
  // ❌ no symlink control — glob may follow symlinked directories
});
```

When a directory like `sdks/typescript` is a symlink to `crates/bindings/typescript`, glob can traverse both paths and return the same physical files under two different relative paths. Each path then becomes a separate `File` node in the graph → duplicate nodes.

---

### Two Layers of Fix (both in `filesystem-walker.ts`)

**Layer 1 — Explicit `follow: false` on glob (primary fix)**

This is the cleanest knob. Glob v11 has a `follow` option; adding it explicitly ensures symlinked directories are not recursively expanded under `**`:

```ts
const files = await glob('**/*', {
  cwd: repoPath,
  nodir: true,
  dot: false,
  follow: false,  // ← prevents traversal into symlinked dirs
});
```

> Note: glob v11 defaults `follow` to `false`, but without being explicit it may behave differently depending on the OS or glob minor version. Spelling it out is safer.

**Layer 2 — Real-path deduplication (belt-and-suspenders)**

Even with `follow: false`, a symlinked *file* (not directory) can still appear. Resolving each path to its canonical form and deduplicating handles all cases:

```ts
// After filtering, deduplicate by real path
const seenRealPaths = new Set<string>();
const deduped: string[] = [];

for (const relativePath of filtered) {
  const fullPath = path.join(repoPath, relativePath);
  try {
    const realPath = await fs.realpath(fullPath);
    if (seenRealPaths.has(realPath)) continue;  // skip duplicate
    seenRealPaths.add(realPath);
    deduped.push(relativePath);
  } catch {
    deduped.push(relativePath);  // fallback: keep the entry
  }
}
// then process `deduped` instead of `filtered`
```

For the SpacetimeDB case (`sdks/typescript` → `crates/bindings/typescript`):
- `crates/bindings/typescript/foo.ts` resolves to real path `/abs/crates/bindings/typescript/foo.ts` → added to set
- `sdks/typescript/foo.ts` resolves to the **same** real path → skipped

---

### Where Exactly to Make Changes

| File | Change |
|------|--------|
| `gitnexus/src/core/ingestion/filesystem-walker.ts` | Add `follow: false` to `glob` call (line 20) + add real-path dedup after the `filter` call (line 26) |
| `gitnexus/src/core/ingestion/pipeline.ts` | No changes needed |
| `gitnexus-web/src/core/ingestion/pipeline.ts` | No changes needed (uses ZIP extraction, not filesystem walking) |

---

### Full Patched `walkRepository`

```ts
export const walkRepository = async (
  repoPath: string,
  onProgress?: (current: number, total: number, filePath: string) => void
): Promise<FileEntry[]> => {
  const files = await glob('**/*', {
    cwd: repoPath,
    nodir: true,
    dot: false,
    follow: false,  // don't traverse into symlinked directories
  });

  const filtered = files.filter(file => !shouldIgnorePath(file));

  // Deduplicate by real path — guards against symlinked files/dirs
  const seenRealPaths = new Set<string>();
  const deduped: string[] = [];
  for (const relativePath of filtered) {
    const fullPath = path.join(repoPath, relativePath);
    try {
      const realPath = await fs.realpath(fullPath);
      if (seenRealPaths.has(realPath)) continue;
      seenRealPaths.add(realPath);
    } catch {
      // realpath failed (broken symlink etc.) — skip it
      continue;
    }
    deduped.push(relativePath);
  }

  const entries: FileEntry[] = [];
  let processed = 0;
  let skippedLarge = 0;

  for (let start = 0; start < deduped.length; start += READ_CONCURRENCY) {
    const batch = deduped.slice(start, start + READ_CONCURRENCY);
    // ... rest unchanged, but use deduped.length for total
  }
  // ...
};
```

> Note: broken symlinks that `realpath` can't resolve are now skipped (they'd fail `readFile` anyway, so this is an improvement).

