### Analysis: Segfault Fix Check

- [x] Gather context from issue
- [x] Check recent git history on `main` for embedding-related changes
- [x] Inspect analyze command code for embedding default settings
- [x] Report findings

---

**Yes, this is fixed in the current `main` (v1.2.8).**

The user's issue shows embeddings were loading automatically (causing the segfault), but in the current codebase **embeddings are disabled by default** and require an explicit `--embeddings` flag.

#### What the code shows now (`gitnexus/src/cli/analyze.ts`):

```typescript
let embeddingSkipped = true;
let embeddingSkipReason = 'off (use --embeddings to enable)';

if (options?.embeddings) {
  if (stats.nodes > EMBEDDING_NODE_LIMIT) {
    embeddingSkipReason = `skipped (${stats.nodes.toLocaleString()} nodes > limit)`;
  } else {
    embeddingSkipped = false;
  }
}

if (!embeddingSkipped) {
  // embedding pipeline only runs here
}
```

The CLI flag is defined in `gitnexus/src/cli/index.ts:30`:
```typescript
.option('--embeddings', 'Enable embedding generation for semantic search (off by default)')
```

#### Summary

| | Before fix (user's report) | After fix (current `main` v1.2.8) |
|---|---|---|
| Default behavior | Embeddings loaded automatically | Embeddings skipped by default |
| Reported output | `Loading embedding model...` → segfault | `off (use --embeddings to enable)` |
| To enable | N/A (always ran) | Pass `--embeddings` flag explicitly |
| Node limit guard | None | Auto-skips if >50,000 nodes even with flag |

The `analyze` command now only loads the embedding model if `--embeddings` is explicitly passed, so the segfault from the `transformers.js` native module should no longer occur on a plain `analyze` run. The user should update to v1.2.8 (`npm install -g gitnexus@1.2.8`) to get the fix.

