### Concrete Phase 2 Sketch

The key structural change: after Phase 2, `resolveLanguageImport` in `import-processor.ts` has an explicit Python branch (like Go/C#/PHP) and `standard.ts` has zero language-specific code:

```typescript
// import-processor.ts — resolveLanguageImport
// Python: proximity-first + PEP 328 (NEW first-class case)
if (language === SupportedLanguages.Python) {
  const resolved = resolvePythonImport(filePath, rawImportPath, ctx.allFilePaths, ctx.allFileList, ctx.normalizedFileList, ctx.index);
  return resolved ? { kind: 'files', files: [resolved] } : null;
}

// ... other languages ...

// Standard fallback (TypeScript/JavaScript path aliases + generic relative + suffix)
const resolvedPath = resolveImportPath(...);
return resolvedPath ? { kind: 'files', files: [resolvedPath] } : null;
```

The `resolvePythonImport` function in `resolvers/python.ts` consolidates everything: PEP 328, proximity, dot-qualified paths, `__init__.py` package detection — and makes them independently testable. The existing unit test (`suffix-index-ambiguity.test.ts`) and integration test (`python.test.ts`) would move to test `resolvePythonImport` directly.

