### Recommended Integration Tests for `fix/mcp-parallel-stability`

The existing test suite has `lbug-pool.test.ts` covering basic lifecycle, parameterized queries, and error handling, but none of the concurrency/parallelism scenarios that this PR specifically fixes. All tests below use the existing `withTestLbugDB` helper and fit naturally into `gitnexus/test/integration/lbug-pool.test.ts` (or a new `lbug-pool-parallel.test.ts`).

---

#### 1. Core Regression: Parallel `executeQuery` calls — `MAX_CONNS_PER_REPO` at once

This is the exact bug from #326. Tests that 8 simultaneous queries (= pool size) all complete without crashing or dropping results.

```typescript
describe('parallel query execution (regression: #326)', () => {
  it('handles MAX_CONNS_PER_REPO parallel executeQuery calls without crash', async () => {
    await initLbug('test-repo', handle.dbPath);
    const PARALLEL = 8; // = MAX_CONNS_PER_REPO
    const results = await Promise.all(
      Array.from({ length: PARALLEL }, () =>
        executeQuery('test-repo', 'MATCH (n:Function) RETURN n.name AS name')
      )
    );
    expect(results).toHaveLength(PARALLEL);
    for (const rows of results) {
      expect(rows.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(2);
    }
  });

  it('handles parallel executeParameterized calls without crash', async () => {
    await initLbug('test-repo', handle.dbPath);
    const results = await Promise.all(
      Array.from({ length: 8 }, (_, i) =>
        executeParameterized(
          'test-repo',
          'MATCH (n:Function) WHERE n.name = $name RETURN n.name AS name',
          { name: i % 2 === 0 ? 'main' : 'helper' }
        )
      )
    );
    expect(results).toHaveLength(8);
    for (const rows of results) {
      expect(Array.isArray(rows)).toBe(true);
    }
  });

  it('handles mixed parallel executeQuery + executeParameterized calls', async () => {
    await initLbug('test-repo', handle.dbPath);
    const results = await Promise.all([
      executeQuery('test-repo', 'MATCH (n:Function) RETURN n.name AS name'),
      executeQuery('test-repo', 'MATCH (n:File) RETURN n.name AS name'),
      executeQuery('test-repo', 'MATCH (n:Function)-[r:CodeRelation]->(m) RETURN n.name AS name'),
      executeParameterized('test-repo', 'MATCH (n:Function) WHERE n.name = $name RETURN n', { name: 'main' }),
      executeQuery('test-repo', 'MATCH (n:Function) RETURN count(n) AS count'),
      executeParameterized('test-repo', 'MATCH (n:Function) WHERE n.isExported = $v RETURN n.name', { v: true }),
    ]);
    expect(results).toHaveLength(6);
    expect(Array.isArray(results[0])).toBe(true);
  });
});
```

---

#### 2. Waiter Queue: More parallel queries than pool connections

Ensures the `waiters` queue path in `checkout()` works correctly — requests that exceed the 8-connection cap queue up and complete when connections are returned via `checkin()`.

```typescript
it('queues requests beyond pool capacity and fulfills them on checkin', async () => {
  await initLbug('test-repo', handle.dbPath);
  // Fire 12 queries against an 8-connection pool — 4 must queue as waiters
  const PARALLEL = 12;
  const results = await Promise.all(
    Array.from({ length: PARALLEL }, () =>
      executeQuery('test-repo', 'MATCH (n:Function) RETURN n.name AS name')
    )
  );
  expect(results).toHaveLength(PARALLEL);
  for (const rows of results) {
    expect(rows.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(2);
  }
});
```

---

#### 3. Concurrent `initLbug` for the Same `repoId` — No Double-Init

Tests the new `initPromises` deduplication guard. Without it, concurrent inits would race past the `pool.get` check, increment `shared.refCount` twice, and the second `pool.set` would silently overwrite and leak the first set of connections.

```typescript
it('concurrent initLbug calls for the same repoId deduplicate correctly', async () => {
  // Fire 6 concurrent inits for the same repoId
  await Promise.all([
    initLbug('test-repo', handle.dbPath),
    initLbug('test-repo', handle.dbPath),
    initLbug('test-repo', handle.dbPath),
    initLbug('test-repo', handle.dbPath),
    initLbug('test-repo', handle.dbPath),
    initLbug('test-repo', handle.dbPath),
  ]);
  expect(isLbugReady('test-repo')).toBe(true);

  // Pool should be fully functional with correct connection count
  // (double-init would corrupt available[] or leak native connections)
  const results = await Promise.all(
    Array.from({ length: 8 }, () =>
      executeQuery('test-repo', 'MATCH (n:Function) RETURN n.name AS name')
    )
  );
  for (const rows of results) {
    expect(rows.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(2);
  }
});
```

---

#### 4. `stdout.write` Is Restored After Parallel Pool Init + Queries

Verifies the stdout silencing/restoration invariant holds under parallel load. If any `silenceStdout`/`restoreStdout` pairing is broken (e.g., from a thrown exception mid-construction), `process.stdout.write` stays as a no-op and MCP responses are silently dropped.

```typescript
it('process.stdout.write is the real write after pool init and parallel queries', async () => {
  const realWrite = process.stdout.write.bind(process.stdout);
  await initLbug('test-repo', handle.dbPath);

  await Promise.all(
    Array.from({ length: 8 }, () =>
      executeQuery('test-repo', 'MATCH (n:Function) RETURN n.name AS name')
    )
  );

  // stdout.write must not be the silenced no-op
  expect(process.stdout.write).not.toEqual(expect.any(Function) && (() => true));
  // And must be callable (not throw)
  expect(() => process.stdout.write('')).not.toThrow();
});
```

---

#### 5. Connection Checkin — No Leaks After Many Sequential Queries

Runs many sequential queries to verify `checkin()` always returns connections to the pool. A leak would eventually exhaust the 8-connection pool and block the 9th caller at the waiter timeout.

```typescript
it('connections are returned to pool after each query (no leaks over 50 sequential queries)', async () => {
  await initLbug('test-repo', handle.dbPath);
  for (let i = 0; i < 50; i++) {
    await executeQuery('test-repo', 'MATCH (n:Function) RETURN n.name AS name');
  }
  // If connections leaked, this parallel batch would hang until WAITER_TIMEOUT_MS
  const results = await Promise.all(
    Array.from({ length: 8 }, () =>
      executeQuery('test-repo', 'MATCH (n:Function) RETURN n.name AS name')
    )
  );
  expect(results).toHaveLength(8);
}, 60_000);
```

---

#### 6. Pool Entry Is Atomic — No Half-Built Pool Visible to Concurrent Queries

Validates that `pool.set()` happens only after pre-warm and FTS load complete, so callers never receive a partial pool entry. An early query (before init completes) must see "not initialized", not a pool with fewer than `MAX_CONNS_PER_REPO` connections.

```typescript
it('executeQuery before initLbug completes sees "not initialized", never a partial pool', async () => {
  // Start init without awaiting
  const initPromise = initLbug('test-repo', handle.dbPath);

  // Immediate query before init resolves — must fail cleanly, not segfault
  const earlyResult = await executeQuery('test-repo', 'MATCH (n:Function) RETURN n')
    .catch((e: Error) => ({ error: e.message }));

  await initPromise;

  if (typeof earlyResult === 'object' && 'error' in earlyResult) {
    // Correct: pool wasn't ready yet
    expect(earlyResult.error).toMatch(/not initialized/);
  } else {
    // Also acceptable: init completed before the synchronous JS turn switched
    expect(Array.isArray(earlyResult)).toBe(true);
  }
});
```

---

#### 7. Pool Integrity Error Is Thrown (Not a Silent `createConnection` Race)

After the PR, if connections are leaked somehow (e.g., `checkin` isn't called), `checkout()` now throws a `Connection pool integrity error` instead of silently calling `createConnection()` (which would silence stdout mid-query). Test this via a mock or by verifying the error message shape.

```typescript
it('pool integrity error is thrown when connection count drops below MAX_CONNS_PER_REPO', async () => {
  // This test validates the guard added in checkout() for the lazy-create code path.
  // We can't easily trigger it without patching internals, so verify the error is
  // descriptive when the pool reports fewer connections than expected.
  // (Primarily a smoke test that the code path compiles and the message is useful.)
  await initLbug('test-repo', handle.dbPath);

  // Verify pool is functional at full capacity
  const rows = await executeQuery('test-repo', 'MATCH (n:Function) RETURN n.name AS name');
  expect(rows.length).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(2);
  // Pool should not throw an integrity error on normal operation
});
```

