### Redundancies Found

#### 1. `detectCursorCLI()` called on every LLM invocation
**File:** `gitnexus/src/core/wiki/cursor-client.ts:66`

```ts
export async function callCursorLLM(...): Promise<LLMResponse> {
  const cursorBin = detectCursorCLI(); // ← re-runs execSync('agent --version') every call
```

`detectCursorCLI()` runs `execSync('agent --version')` on **every single wiki page generation**. It's already called once at the start of the interactive setup flow (`wiki.ts:172`). This doubles as a correctness guard inside `callCursorLLM`, but it means N extra `execSync` forks for N wiki pages. The result should be passed through or cached.

[Fix this →](https://claude.ai/code?q=In%20gitnexus%2Fsrc%2Fcore%2Fwiki%2Fcursor-client.ts%2C%20the%20detectCursorCLI%28%29%20function%20is%20called%20on%20every%20callCursorLLM%20invocation%20%28line%2066%29%2C%20running%20execSync%28%27agent%20--version%27%29%20for%20each%20wiki%20page.%20Cache%20the%20result%20module-level%20or%20accept%20the%20binary%20path%20as%20a%20parameter%20to%20avoid%20redundant%20shell%20forks.&repo=abhigyanpatwari/GitNexus)

#### 2. Two separate verbose/debug env-var mechanisms
**Files:** `wiki.ts:86-88` and `wiki.ts:470`

```ts
// --verbose sets GITNEXUS_VERBOSE
if (options?.verbose) {
  process.env.GITNEXUS_VERBOSE = '1';
}

// ...but full error stack traces check a *different* var:
if (process.env.DEBUG) {
  console.error(err);
}
```

Two unrelated env vars control logging: `GITNEXUS_VERBOSE` for cursor CLI debug output, `DEBUG` for error stack traces. `--verbose` doesn't enable `DEBUG`, so verbose users get cursor CLI spawn details but not stack traces on errors. Consider aliasing `--verbose` to also set `DEBUG` or unifying behind one var.

[Fix this →](https://claude.ai/code?q=In%20gitnexus%2Fsrc%2Fcli%2Fwiki.ts%2C%20the%20--verbose%20flag%20sets%20GITNEXUS_VERBOSE%20%28line%2087%29%20but%20error%20stack%20traces%20are%20gated%20on%20process.env.DEBUG%20%28line%20470%29.%20When%20--verbose%20is%20active%2C%20also%20enable%20DEBUG%20or%20emit%20stack%20traces%20directly%20so%20verbose%20mode%20is%20comprehensive.&repo=abhigyanpatwari/GitNexus)

#### 3. Config saved then immediately re-read via `resolveLLMConfig`
**File:** `wiki.ts:125-152`

```ts
// Block 1: save CLI overrides to disk
await saveCLIConfig({ ...existing, ...updates });

// Block 2: resolveLLMConfig re-reads from disk + env vars
let llmConfig = await resolveLLMConfig({ model, baseUrl, apiKey, provider });
```

The overrides are written to `~/.gitnexus/config.json`, then `resolveLLMConfig` reads them back. The two-pass write→read pattern works but is unnecessary; `resolveLLMConfig` already accepts the overrides directly. The save is useful for persistence, but `llmConfig` could be built purely from the passed overrides without the disk roundtrip for the current session.

#### 4. `WikiOptions` doesn't carry `verbose`; it's wired via env var instead
**File:** `wiki.ts:286-292` vs `generator.ts:66-75`

```ts
// wiki.ts — verbose is NOT passed through to WikiOptions
const wikiOptions: WikiOptions = {
  force: options?.force,
  model: options?.model,
  // verbose: missing — threaded via process.env instead
};
```

This works but is implicit. `WikiOptions` and `WikiGenerator` are unaware of verbose mode; they rely on `cursor-client.ts` reading `process.env.GITNEXUS_VERBOSE`. If the generator is ever called programmatically (e.g. from tests or another library), callers can't enable verbose output without mutating the environment.

