## `html-viewer.ts` — Script Injection Fix

### What the fix does
`escapeForScript` replaces `</` → `<\/` in JSON embedded inside `<script>` blocks, preventing the HTML parser from treating `</script>` inside markdown content as the end of the script tag.

### Issues

**1. Incomplete HTML injection escaping (minor)**

`<\/` escaping handles `</script>` but misses two additional vectors that can terminate script blocks in some parsers:
- `<!--` in legacy IE and certain XML parsers can trigger SGML comment parsing inside `<script>`
- `]]>` for XHTML/CDATA contexts

The gold standard (used by React, Django, etc.) is to unicode-escape `<`, `>`, and `&`:
```typescript
// Current (only handles </script>)
const escapeForScript = (s: string) => s.replace(/<\//g, '<\\/');

// Safer alternative
const escapeForScript = (s: string) =>
  s.replace(/</g, '\\u003c').replace(/>/g, '\\u003e').replace(/&/g, '\\u0026');
```
Unicode escapes are valid JSON string content and completely neutralize HTML parser interference. [Fix this →](https://claude.ai/code?q=In%20gitnexus%2Fsrc%2Fcore%2Fwiki%2Fhtml-viewer.ts%20on%20branch%20fix%2Fwiki-script-escape-and-llm-token-param%2C%20line%2071%2C%20change%20the%20escapeForScript%20function%20from%20replacing%20only%20%22%3C%2F%22%20to%20replacing%20%22%3C%22%20with%20%22%5Cu003c%22%2C%20%22%3E%22%20with%20%22%5Cu003e%22%2C%20and%20%22%26%22%20with%20%22%5Cu0026%22%20for%20more%20complete%20HTML%20injection%20protection.&repo=abhigyanpatwari/GitNexus)

**2. `null` meta case is safe (no issue)**
`JSON.stringify(null)` produces `"null"` which contains no `</` — this works correctly.

**3. Fix is consistent with existing code (good)**
Lines 85 and 122 already use `'<\/script>'` string literals with the same escaping style. ✅

---

## `llm-client.ts` — Token Parameter Compatibility

### What the fix does
- Adds `tokenParamStyle` to `LLMConfig` for explicit override
- Auto-detects o-series models via regex and uses `max_completion_tokens`
- Adds a retry fallback that swaps the parameter name on 400 errors

### Issues

**1. Bug: `tokenParamStyle` is silently dropped in `resolveLLMConfig`** (lines 44–57)

The override is accepted in the `LLMConfig` interface but `resolveLLMConfig` never copies it into the returned config:

```typescript
return {
  apiKey,
  baseUrl: ...,
  model: ...,
  maxTokens: overrides?.maxTokens ?? 16_384,
  temperature: overrides?.temperature ?? 0,
  // tokenParamStyle from overrides is LOST here
};
```

A caller doing `resolveLLMConfig({ tokenParamStyle: 'max_completion_tokens' })` gets back a config with `tokenParamStyle: undefined`. [Fix this →](https://claude.ai/code?q=In%20gitnexus%2Fsrc%2Fcore%2Fwiki%2Fllm-client.ts%20on%20branch%20fix%2Fwiki-script-escape-and-llm-token-param%2C%20the%20resolveLLMConfig%20function%20(lines%2044-57)%20does%20not%20include%20tokenParamStyle%20in%20the%20returned%20config%20object.%20Add%20%22tokenParamStyle%3A%20overrides%3F.tokenParamStyle%2C%22%20to%20the%20returned%20object.&repo=abhigyanpatwari/GitNexus)

**2. Regex false-positive risk on arbitrary model names** (line 74)

```typescript
const MAX_COMPLETION_TOKENS_MODELS = /\b(o1|o3|o4)(-mini|-preview|-pro)?\b/i;
```

`\b` matches at a non-word/word boundary, so `some-o1-finetune` or `provider/o1-clone` would match. Current real-world OpenAI model IDs (`o1`, `o1-mini`, `o1-preview`, `o3`, `o3-mini`, `o4-mini`) all work correctly, but a more conservative pattern would anchor to the start of the model name or path segment:

```typescript
// Only match when o1/o3/o4 is at start or after a path separator
const MAX_COMPLETION_TOKENS_MODELS = /(?:^|[\/])o(1|3|4)(-mini|-preview|-pro)?\b/i;
```

**3. Retry swap could burn all 3 attempts on parameter negotiation** (lines 131–140)

With `MAX_RETRIES = 3`: if attempt 0 uses `max_tokens`, gets a 400 swap → attempt 1 uses `max_completion_tokens`, gets another 400 swap back → attempt 2 is the last retry. Only 1 attempt remains for actual transient failures. This is bounded by the guards (`!body.max_completion_tokens`, `!body.max_tokens`) so an infinite loop isn't possible, but a genuinely unreachable endpoint would take 3 swap attempts before failing, exhausting retries without useful backoff.

**4. No env var support for `tokenParamStyle`** (minor / by design?)

`GITNEXUS_MODEL`, `GITNEXUS_LLM_BASE_URL`, etc. all have env var equivalents, but `tokenParamStyle` doesn't. A `GITNEXUS_TOKEN_PARAM_STYLE` env var would let CLI users configure this without code. Low priority if this is intentionally a programmatic-only override.

**5. Auto-detection logic is clean and idiomatic ✅**

The `style === 'auto'` branch correctly defers to regex detection, and explicit overrides (`'max_tokens'` / `'max_completion_tokens'`) bypass detection entirely. Good design.

