#### 3. Redundant `graph` dep alongside `nodeById` — `GraphCanvas.tsx:70,79,121`

```tsx
// GraphCanvas.tsx:63-70
const handleNodeClick = useCallback((nodeId: string) => {
    if (!graph) return;  // ← redundant: nodeById is empty Map when graph is null
    const node = nodeById.get(nodeId);
    // ...
}, [graph, nodeById, setSelectedNode, openCodePanel]); // ← `graph` is redundant
```

`nodeById` is derived from `graph` via `useMemo([graph])`. When `graph` is null, `nodeById` is already an empty `Map`, so `nodeById.get()` returns `undefined` and the `if (node)` guard handles it. The `if (!graph) return` guard and the `graph` dep in the callback are both redundant. Same pattern repeated in `handleNodeHover` (L79) and `useImperativeHandle` (L121). Minor, but adds noise.

